Companion change for fold-run/fold.

This repo's build output moved from `console/` to `dist/`. fold's
scripts/sync-console.sh is the only thing in fold that reads that directory
name — the Makefile targets, ci.yml's `console` job and the weekly
console-sync workflow all go through the script — so this is the whole
fold-side change.

  cd /path/to/fold
  git apply /path/to/fold-console/docs/fold-sync-console.patch

Then bump the pin, in the SAME commit, to the fold-console commit that did the
rename:

  sed -i '' "s/CONSOLE_COMMIT:-[0-9a-f]\{40\}/CONSOLE_COMMIT:-<40-hex>/" scripts/sync-console.sh
  make sync-console          # re-vendors gateway/console + console_source.go
  make console-check         # must be clean
  go test ./gateway -run 'Console|Introspection'

The patch does not carry the pin, because a placeholder SHA in a supply-chain
pin is worse than an obvious missing step.

WHY THEY MUST LAND TOGETHER
The script and the pin describe the same upstream layout. Split them and the
sync fails loudly in either direction — a pre-rename pin has no dist/, a
post-rename one has no console/ — so the failure mode is a red build, never
silently vendored stale bytes. Note this also means the weekly console-sync
workflow will fail to open its PR from the moment fold-console's main carries
the rename until this patch lands. That is the intended order of operations,
not a regression to debug.

The embedded file set is unchanged: index.html, app.js, style.css and the four
font subsets plus OFL.txt come out of the new build under exactly the names
MANIFEST already lists, so gateway/introspection_test.go needs no change.

